    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br><br>On Tuesday, August 5, 2014 9:53:29 PM UTC-4, KangMin Ngo wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;d like to plot a map of my seed and seedling traps, with the positions in &#39;x&#39; and &#39;y&#39;, and a colour scheme based on &#39;count&#39;. The &#39;seedling&#39; plots are slightly larger than the &#39;seed&#39; plots, which I&#39;ve managed to do in the code below. </div><div><br></div><div>The colour scheme has to have 2 different colours for &#39;seed&#39; and &#39;seedling&#39;, but I haven&#39;t managed to get it to work using scale_colour_brewer(). I think I&#39;m just missing a small clue, can anyone help me? </div><div><br></div><div><div>p &lt;- ggplot(data, aes(x,y)) + geom_point(aes(colour=count, size=type), shape=15)</div><div><br></div><div>p + scale_size_manual(values=c(2, 3)) + scale_colour_brewer(???)</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"325\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:325pt\">\r\n\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"65\" span=\"5\" style=\"width:65pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" width=\"65\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:65pt\">x</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">y</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">trap</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">count</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">type</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" align=\"right\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">35</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">50</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">20</td>\r\n  <td>seed</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" align=\"right\" style=\"height:15.0pt\"